            "verified": true,
            "ms": 3378,
            "answer": "It is foolish to wish that your family and friends live forever because you are wishing for things to be in your power which are not so, and what belongs to others to be your own. This is an exercise in wishing for what is beyond your control, which leads to disappointment. Instead, one should exercise what is within their own power to avoid such disappointment [1]."
